  "prompt": "Are PEZA-registered enterprises subject to corporate income tax?",
  "runtimeCommit": "d71b913ddf39726234dd02d858fac3e5275e865b",
  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nAre PEZA-registered enterprises subject to corporate income tax in the Philippines?\n\n### Short Answer\nYes, PEZA-registered enterprises are generally subject to corporate income tax, but they may benefit from preferential tax rates or exemptions under specific conditions.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe primary authority governing corporate income tax is Section 27 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which outlines the rates of income tax on domestic corporations. Additionally, Section 24 of the NIRC provides the general framework for income tax rates applicable to corporations.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nPEZA-registered enterprises should assess their eligibility for preferential tax rates or exemptions based on their compliance with PEZA requirements and the nature of their business activities. It is advisable for these enterprises to maintain accurate records and documentation to support their claims for any tax incentives. Consulting with a tax professional or legal advisor familiar with PEZA regulations can also help ensure compliance and optimize tax liabilities.",
